   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT providing for a property taxpayer assistance authorization for taxpayers in the town of Henrietta, county of Monroe",
    "basePrintNo": "S7109",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7109-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Monroe County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7109\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act providing for a property taxpayer assistance\nauthorization for taxpayers in the town of Henrietta, county of Monroe\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill authorizes the town of Henrietta, county of Monroe, to grant\na property taxpayer assistance payment of $100 to qualified taxpayers\nwithin the town limits for fiscal year 2014.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the town of Henrietta to adopt and amend local\nlaws in accordance with this section to grant a property taxpayer\nassistance payment to certain taxpayers. This section also states the\neligibility requirements for the property tax assistance payment.\n\nSection 2 states that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe town of Henrietta has developed an unreserved, general fund\nsurplus through sound fiscal management. The town board wishes to\nprovide tax relief to residential property owners in the form of a\npayment of $100 in an effort to alleviate the property tax burden on\nits residents.\n\nIn order to qualify, the recipient must be a property taxpayer in the\ntown of Henrietta on June 1, 2014, not be in arrears in the payment of\ntaxes, charges, or assessments due and owing to the town, and the\nproperty must serve as the primary residence of one or more of the\nowners.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
